## DESCRIPTION
## Smooth manifolds and implicit form
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Smooth manifolds and implicit form')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "parserPopUp.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

$mc = PopUp(["?", "Yes", "No"], "Yes");

BEGIN_PGML


Let [` F : \mathbb{R}^5 \to \mathbb{R}^3 `] be a [` C^1 `] map. Fix a point [` p \in \mathbb{R}^5 `]. You have calculated that

>>[` F(p) = \begin{bmatrix} 0\\0\\0 \end{bmatrix}, \quad DF(p) = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 & 3 \end{bmatrix} \quad \text{and} \quad \mathrm{rref}(DF(p)) = \begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \end{bmatrix} `].<<

Is the set [` S = F^{-1}( \{ (0,0,0) \}) `] a smooth manifold at [` p `]? [_]{$mc}

If so, of what dimension? Enter 0 if the previous answer is no. [_]{Real(2)}
END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();